lem" "value" "Consider the line $y=-\\frac{2}{3}x-3$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=-81.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/state.json" "file_sha256" "5eea7e91a9abc0d58092dce40dc68afaebe713a32d097ba5407f3506df1c80f1" "basis" 869 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-281130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the line $y=-\\frac{2}{3}x-3$ passes through the points $A(0,-3)$ and $B(3,-5)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 7 \\\\ -6 & -13\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(-3,-6)$ and ${B}^{′}(7,-13).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y+6 & =\\frac{-13+6}{7-(-3)}(x+3) \\\\ y+6 & =-\\frac{7}{10}(x+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10y+60 & =-7x-21 \\\\ 7x+10y & =-81\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/state.json" "file_sha256" "5eea7e91a9abc0d58092dce40dc68afaebe713a32d097ba5407f3506df1c80f1" "basis" 869 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-281130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1c51e49536a811c52da04573453ecaf29d405a6bb4368af15d5a0ff0c364ff3f" "basis" 869 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-281130" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/state.json" "file_sha256" "5eea7e91a9abc0d58092dce40dc68afaebe713a32d097ba5407f3506df1c80f1" "basis" 869 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-281130" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7x+10y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/state.json" "file_sha256" "5eea7e91a9abc0d58092dce40dc68afaebe713a32d097ba5407f3506df1c80f1" "basis" 869 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the line $y=-x-4$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/state.json" "file_sha256" "5eea7e91a9abc0d58092dce40dc68afaebe713a32d097ba5407f3506df1c80f1" "basis" 869 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the line $y=-x-4$ passes through the points $W(0,-4)$ and $Z(1,-5)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $W$ and $Z$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${W}^{′}(8,0)$ and ${Z}^{′}(9,-3).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${W}^{′}$ and ${Z}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-0 & =\\frac{-3-0}{9-8}(x-8) \\\\ y & =-3(x-8) \\\\ y & =-3x+24 \\\\ 3x+y-24 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/state.json" "file_sha256" "5eea7e91a9abc0d58092dce40dc68afaebe713a32d097ba5407f3506df1c80f1" "basis" 869 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1c51e49536a811c52da04573453ecaf29d405a6bb4368af15d5a0ff0c364ff3f" "basis" 869 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77779" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/state.json" "file_sha256" "5eea7e91a9abc0d58092dce40dc68afaebe713a32d097ba5407f3506df1c80f1" "basis" 869 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77779" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x+y+24=0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/state.json" "file_sha256" "5eea7e91a9abc0d58092dce40dc68afaebe713a32d097ba5407f3506df1c80f1" "basis" 869 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77779" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x+y-24=0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/state.json" "file_sha256" "5eea7e91a9abc0d58092dce40dc68afaebe713a32d097ba5407f3506df1c80f1" "basis" 869 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77779" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x+y-8=0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980539/state.json" "file_sha256" "5eea7e91a9abc0d58092dce40dc68afaebe713a32d097ba5407f3506df1c80f1" "basis